From 83947b4e43301881e752873b5067198774533fbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:40:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: Dolby Vision sent as HDR10+, version 1
 carries DistributionY99 and DistributionY100nit

In application version 1 the places of 5 and 10 % of the HDR10+
InfoFrame are not percentiles of maxRGB. The HDR10+ LLC specification,
as quietvoid quoted it in the CoreELEC forum (thread 51770, post 369),
defines them as:
 - DistributionY99: the highest, in the scene, of the 99.99th
   percentile of the linear luminance of each picture;
 - DistributionY100nit: the average, in the scene, of the percentage
   (0 to 100) of the pixels of each picture whose luminance is at most
   100 cd/m2.
1.0 RC5 put the percentiles of maxRGB there. The place of 10 % goes in
the InfoFrame as it is coded in version 1, so about 30 cd/m2 (300)
was clamped to 255, where a licensed player sends 78 to 100 for the
same kind of film (cinema-ONE, three films measured on its HDMI output,
issue 10). The specification itself is given to adopters only and is
not here: the definitions are taken from that quote.

The samples of the GPU now carry the luminance of each sample too
(BT.2020, 0.2627 R + 0.6780 G + 0.0593 B of the linear R, G and B,
SMPTE ST 2084 each way, as a 16-bit PQ code), from the same pixels as
maxRGB: one sample per texel of the target, four bytes, where it held
two samples of two bytes. maxRGB is computed as before, so its codes
do not change. The module keeps, per scene, the highest 99.99th
percentile of a picture and the average of the percentages, and puts
them in those two places in version 1; version 0 keeps its nine
percentiles of maxRGB and its decisions, which are the same as before
(dvbridge_dvplus_set_version(0)). In version 1 a move of one of the two
values counts as a move of what is sent, as a move of a percentile
does (DistributionY100nit, a percentage, by more than 2 points, and by
more than 10 to change before the interval; chosen, not measured).
Provisional statistics from a level 1 block make both of that function
taken as the luminance (an upper bound of DistributionY99, a lower one
of DistributionY100nit). kodi.log gives both values with the first
metadata sent and every 240 pictures.

Titles differ in the place of 5 %: hdr10plus_tool's samples carry a
value near the peak there, as the definition has it, and the three
films of the licensed player one between their 1 and 25 %. The
definition is followed.
